{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>וכי יזיד.</b> Its meaning is to kill him, as if it were written והרגו בערמה, and like it כי תחל לזנות (Leviticus 21:9), which means כי תחלל נפשה לזנות, therefore her father profanes her [תחללת]. It is known that the language of חלול and also of תחלה are from the doubled [binyanim] and they are two meanings, therefore it was necessary to distinguish between the two. He said כי תֵחֵל לזנות, for from the language of תחלה one says תָחֵל, like תָחֵל לספור (Deuteronomy 16:9)." "<b>מעם מזבחי.</b> This is the opposite of the first verse, where it is written ושמתי לך מקום, and these are the cities of refuge. Only the intentional killer — he shall flee even from My altar, as Joab did — shall be put to death. And our predecessors said: even a priest who wishes to perform the service of My altar shall be put to death."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "Resolved the two 1 Kings 2:5 cross-references implied by כאשר עשה יואב and by וקדמונינו אמרו (b. Yoma 85a) implicitly; kept Ibn Ezra's argument about חלל/תחל in literal form as he presents it."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:57.031771710Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}